s. You need one more winner. "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["ls","nc"],["hs","nh"],["at","There are two suits that can easily provide the extra trick - the Hearts "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["hs","ss"],["at","or the Spades. In either suit, you can take a finesse against the King by leading low toward the Ace-Queen. Even if the finesse loses, you will still have established the Jack as your ninth trick. Which suit should you play?"],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","wd"],["nt","\nTo win on this hand, you must watch the opponents. West has led a Diamond. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hc","da"],["at","Once your @DA is dislodged, "],["pg",""],["lc","da"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","da"],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["at","the opponents will have established the Diamonds as winning tricks. "],["pg",""],["hs","ed"],["at","If, as above, the Diamonds are divided 5-3, the opponents will be poised to take four tricks and defeat your contract if you let them win another trick."],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["up","1"],["nt","\nTo prevent the opponents from being able to take all of their tricks, you can start by using the hold-up play. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","sd"],["at","Don't win the first "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","sd"],["at","or second trick, "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","dq"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hc","da"],["at","but wait until the third trick to take your @DA. "],["pg",""],["lc","da"],["pc","dj"],["pc","s"],["pc","d"],["pc","da"],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["hs","ed"],["at","If the suit is divided 5-3, "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["at","East will not have any Diamonds left. You have created one safe opponent, East, "],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["hs","wd"],["at","and one dangerous opponent, West."],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","nh"],["nt","\nNow it is easy to see that you should develop your extra trick in Hearts "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["hs","ss"],["at","rather than Spades. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","sh"],["at","You can lead a small Heart from your hand "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["hc","hq"],["at","to dummy's @HQ. "],["pg",""],["lc","hq"],["pc","hq"],["md","0,hk,,h7"],["hc","hk"],["at","If West has the @HK, "],["pg",""],["lc","hk"],["hs","eh"],["at","your @HQ will win "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["at","and you will have enough tricks to make your contract. You could even use an entry back to your hand "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["ls","nc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ca"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["hs","sh"],["at","and repeat the finesse "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","hj"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["at","for an overtrick."],["pg",""],["md","0,h7,,hk"],["up","9"],["hs","eh"],["nt","\nIf, as above, the finesse loses to East, "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["pc","hk"],["pg",""],["hs","ed"],["at","the contract is safe. East is the safe opponent - he has no more Diamonds left. "],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["hc","hj"],["at","You will be able to win whatever suit East leads back and your @HJ will have been established as your ninth trick."],["pg",""],["lc","hj"],["up","4"],["tc","c"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!c"],["pc","!c"],["tc","r"],["hs","ss"],["nt","\nLook at the difference if you try to set up your extra trick in Spades. "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hc","sk"],["at","If West has the @SK, "],["pg",""],["lc","sk"],["hs","ss"],["hs","ns"],["at","your finesse "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["ls","ns"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sq"],["hs","ws"],["at","will lose "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["pc","sk"],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["at","and you will have let the dangerous opponent on lead. West will be able to take his remaining two Diamond tricks and defeat your contract."],["",""]]}}